---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Useful Links"
  description="A collection of resourceful links and lecture notes for physicists."
>
  <article class="container links-page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker mono">Links</p>
      <h1>Useful Links</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Beginning from research articles to lecture notes and some quick numerical
        tricks for computational physics, I have posted links to things on the
        internet that I've found resourceful as a physicist.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        <strong>Note:</strong> I try my best to keep links updated from time to time.
        In case you find something missing or broken, sorry about that — just try
        googling! If there's something seriously wrong, please drop me an email.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Articles and Essays</h2>
      <p>
        A list of thought-provoking articles and essays relating to different aspects
        of science and research, that I revisit quite frequently for inspiration.
      </p>
      <ul class="link-list">
        <li><a href="https://science.sciencemag.org/content/177/4047/393" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"More is different"</a> — Phil Anderson</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.pnas.org/content/97/1/28" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"Theory of Everything"</a> — Robert Laughlin and David Pines</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cs.virginia.edu/~robins/YouAndYourResearch.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"You and your research"</a> — Richard Hamming</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.ams.org/notices/200902/rtx090200212p.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"Birds and Frogs"</a> — Freeman Dyson</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Lecture Notes &amp; Videos</h2>
      <p>
        Frankly, there are way too many of these online. I've only listed resources
        that I've found exceptionally useful and have something unique to offer.
      </p>
      <ul class="link-list">
        <li>
          <a href="http://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/teaching.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lectures on Theoretical Physics</a>
          — David Tong
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="http://www.tcm.phy.cam.ac.uk/~bds10/grad_lec.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Quantum Condensed Matter Physics</a>
          — Ben Simons
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.perimeterinstitute.ca/training/perimeter-scholars-international/lectures/2011/2012-psi-lectures" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PSI Masters Lecture Videos 2011/2012</a>
          — Perimeter Institute<br />
          <span class="note-inline">Particularly: Mathematical Physics (Carl Bender), Statistical Physics (Leo Kadanoff), Condensed Matter Physics (Nandini Trivedi).</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          Lectures on Quantum Theory — Frederic Schuller
          (<a href="https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLPH7f_7ZlzxQVx5jRjbfRGEzWY_upS5K6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lectures</a> |
          <a href="http://mathswithphysics.blogspot.com/2016/07/frederic-schullers-lectures-on-quantum.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Notes</a>)
        </li>
        <li>
          Lectures on Geometric Anatomy of Theoretical Physics — Frederic Schuller
          (<a href="https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLPH7f_7ZlzxTi6kS4vCmv4ZKm9u8g5yic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lectures</a> |
          <a href="http://mathswithphysics.blogspot.com/2016/07/lectures-on-geometric-anatomy-of.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Notes</a>)
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Software and Scientific Computing</h2>
      <p>
        At times solving problems in physics requires a bit of skill to get computers
        to do things for you. Here I share things I've had the chance to dabble with
        in my research.
      </p>
      <ul class="link-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Simulation / Numerics:</strong>
          <a href="https://www.mathworks.com/products/matlab.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MATLAB</a> |
          <a href="https://www.wolfram.com/mathematica/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mathematica</a> (especially for symbolic calculations)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.wolframalpha.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wolfram Alpha</a>
          — quick math intuition online
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Programming Languages:</strong>
          <a href="https://fortran-lang.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fortran</a> |
          <a href="https://www.python.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Python</a>
          (<a href="https://www.anaconda.com/products/individual" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Anaconda</a>) |
          <a href="https://julialang.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Julia</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.scipy.org/about.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SciPy</a>
          — scientific computing tools for Python
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.netlib.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">netlib</a>
          — Fortran and C package library for science
          (<a href="http://www.moreisdifferent.com/2015/07/16/why-physicsts-still-use-fortran/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Why physicists still use Fortran?</a>)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.latex-project.org/about/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LaTeX</a>
          — for typesetting equations and drafting papers.
          Editors: Texmaker, TeXstudio,
          <a href="https://www.overleaf.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Overleaf</a> (online)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/Reference-LAPACK/lapack" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reference-LAPACK</a>
          on GitHub |
          <a href="https://ctan.org/?lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CTAN</a> — LaTeX package archive
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Text editors:</strong>
          <a href="https://www.sublimetext.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sublime Text</a> |
          <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">VS Code</a> |
          <a href="https://www.vim.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vim</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://spack.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spack</a>
          — a package manager for HPC
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/presentation/scf-convergence-and-diis/notebooks/scf-convergence-and-diis-notebook.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">My interactive notes on SCF convergence and DIIS</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .links-page { padding-top: 3rem; }
  .page-head { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .page-head h1 { margin: 0.2rem 0 0.6rem; }
  .kicker {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .lead { font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 64ch; }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  section { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  section h2 { margin-top: 0; }

  .link-list {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .link-list li { line-height: 1.6; }

  .note-inline {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }
</style>
